{"shortDescription":"The Australian dollar fell below $0.70, hitting a two-week low after higher unemployment and unexpected job cuts in September prompted traders to scale back bets on further rate hikes.The jobless rate came in at 4.7%, above the 4.6% forecast, while the previous month's reading was revised up from a…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The Australian dollar fell below $0.70, hitting a two-week low after higher unemployment and unexpected job cuts in September prompted traders to scale back bets on further rate hikes."]},{"type":"p","children":["The jobless rate came in at 4.7%, above the 4.6% forecast, while the previous month's reading was revised up from an initial 4.6%."]},{"type":"p","children":["The economy also shed 39,300 jobs, compared with expectations for a 20,000 gain, although full-time employment climbed by 34,400."]},{"type":"p","children":["The figures suggested the labor market may be loosening after the Reserve Bank of Australia raised its cash rate by 1 percentage point to 4.60% this year to rein in inflation, marking one of the most aggressive tightening cycles among developed economies."]},{"type":"p","children":["Markets now see less than a 20% chance of a November hike, down from 35% earlier in the day, while the odds of a December move fell to 40% from 60%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Rate markets have also pushed back expectations for further tightening, with May 2027 carrying the highest implied probability of a hike at 80%."]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Forex","args":[{"id":"category","value":"forex"}]},{"title":"Trading Economics","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"trading-economics"}]}],"id":"te_news:592095:0","title":"Australian Dollar Falls to Two-Week Low","published":1792027262,"urgency":2,"link":"https://tradingeconomics.com/australia/currency","permission":"preview","relatedSymbols":[{"symbol":"FX:AUDUSD","currency-logoid":"country/US","base-currency-logoid":"country/AU",